## 12. ACCESSIBILITY — FOLLOW WCAG BEST PRACTICES

Target WCAG 2.2 AA practices wherever applicable.

Requirements:

- Semantic landmarks.
- Correct heading hierarchy.
- Accessible navigation.
- Full keyboard operation.
- Visible focus indicators.
- Sufficient color contrast.
- Accessible labels for all form controls.
- Helpful validation errors.
- Accessible dialogs and drawers.
- Correct focus handling when opening and closing modals.
- Escape-to-close where appropriate.
- Meaningful button names.
- Accessible product selectors.
- No interaction available only through hover.
- Screen-reader-friendly cart and wishlist feedback.
- Respect reduced motion.
- Avoid using color as the only indication of selection or errors.
- Use proper status messages for dynamic changes.
- Ensure text remains readable at increased zoom.

Do not remove outlines without replacing them with a clearly visible focus style.

Use automated accessibility checks and manual keyboard testing.

