## 14. SECURITY AND FORM HANDLING

Never expose secret API keys, private tokens, or credentials in client-side code.

Never collect payment-card details in a custom demo form without a proper payment provider.

Use server-side validation for real submissions and authenticated actions when a backend is introduced.

Frontend validation is not a substitute for server validation.

Do not create fake authentication, fake order confirmation, or fake subscription success messages that imply real server-side operations have occurred.

Keep all demo limitations clearly identified.

